    "created_at": "2026-11-25T05:56:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T05:56:33Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/3333-sinker-start-exit · PR #3980 · pinned by `start_exit_shared::sinker::a_circular_orbit_starts_at_the_start_pick_and_ends_at_the_exit_pick`, `sinker::a_planetary_orbit_reaches_its_radius_at_the_start_pick`, `sinker::a_vector_orbit_starts_on_the_picked_vector_and_ends_on_the_exit_vector`, `sinker::a_pick_that_the_orbit_cannot_hold_is_refused_by_name`, `sinker::a_picked_orbit_keeps_the_undersize_law_and_the_cavity_limits`, `sinker::side::a_side_burn_starts_and_ends_at_the_picked_ends_of_its_side_move`, `sinker::side::a_side_burn_pick_at_the_middle_of_the_move_is_refused_by_name`, `sinker::side::the_generator_refuses_an_impossible_sinker_pick_by_name`, `sinker::side::mcp_edit_operation_sets_the_sinker_picks_and_refuses_an_impossible_one_by_name` · merges when reviewed\n\nWhere the issue is silent, the PR took these readings. The maintainer decides if they are correct.\n\n- The orbit ends at the exit angle. Then the electrode feeds back to the burn position and retracts up the burn axis, as before.\n- A vector orbit keeps its directions. A pick changes the order only, and a pick between two vectors is refused.\n- \"The side where the side move begins\" is read as an end of the side move: the burn position or the wall end.\n\nThe decision file is `docs/decisions/3333-sinker-start-exit.md`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
